  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>In Brignoles, Restaurant Le Jardin offers fine dining/bistronomic cuisine with fresh, seasonal produce, listed by the Gault&Millau guide, in a town-centre garden with around forty outdoor tables (wifi available). A Tripadvisor review explicitly confirms sitting on the terrace with a dog ("We sat in the terrace with a dog") — a customer confirmation that, combined with Gault&Millau's description of the setting, gives a good level of confidence for a restaurant of this standard, where pets aren't always guaranteed a welcome. The restaurant is also very highly rated: 5/5 on Tripadvisor, 3rd out of 55 restaurants in Brignoles (101 reviews).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The hours are tight: service on Tuesday as well as Thursday to Saturday from 12pm to 2pm, with an extra evening service Thursday to Saturday from 7:30pm to 10pm. Closed Monday, Wednesday and Sunday. Expect €17 for the dish of the day, or a €25 lunch menu (€22 for the main course alone). Given the fine-dining format and small dining room, it's best to book ahead.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: book ahead, mention that you're coming with your dog, and aim for the terrace to stay comfortable during service.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Brignoles and the heart of the Provence Verte are right around, a good base if you're exploring the Var backcountry with your dog.</p>
